                                                    3
 SPS’s thermal units are at or near retirement. In addition, planning-reserve margin requirements

within the Southwest Power Pool have dramatically increased.

       10.    SPS and its customers have an urgent need for new generation to ensure SPS is able

to serve new load, fulfill its duty to customers, and meet its obligations. Commission approval of

this Stipulation is urgently needed to ensure SPS can continue its efforts to assure it will have the

resources it needs to adequately and reliably serve its customers.



       Wherefore, Targa prays for Commission to adopt orders necessary to enact the terms of the

Stipulation to support SPS’s efforts to construct and operate new generation resources and related

measures, along with the agreed reasonable customer protections, and to grant all other further

relief as this Commission deems just and proper.



